    "created_at": "2025-10-07T12:59:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-07T12:59:42Z",
    "body": "As I'm continuing to dig through Chromium's implementation, I'm now less convinced that this is a feasible idea: I was simply wrong about how often `.origin` returns something other than a serialized origin. At least `MessagePort.postMessage` (whose implementation is also used by workers) doesn't set an `origin` when constructing a `MessageEvent` (step 7.7 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#message-port-post-message-steps). This means that we're not just talking about the (probably small) number of userland-constructed `MessageEvent` objects, but also a pretty common scenario whose events developers might be examining.\n\nSoooo... I'm just going to quietly close this and do more research before making more clever suggestions. :)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
